  "choices": [
    "Adopt brokestar complete16-dye paint policy and original GT6 color order/RGBs into shared PaintingRules, PaintState and primitive Paintable contract. Both versions actually consume dye conversion, per-channel average mixing, sheep/tamed-wolf entity facts and six-dye grass mappings. Register32 new gregtech:spray_paint_<color> and _2 full/used identities through existing GTMultiItems registries; reuse Source1 empty_spray_can and paint_removal_spray/_2. Original1281 multi-items remain, total1313. Retain the coherent Source1 full/used/empty ledger rather than importing brokestar separate gt6 empty/remover or another consumable root.",
    "Native and Forge PaintSprayItem use existing ItemBehaviors.Consumable with gt.remaining,5120 internal capacity,10 block cost/50 entity cost, actual full→used→empty swaps, creative exemption and13-pixel color/remaining bar. Full brokestar block whitelist: plain/stained glass and panes, plain/stained terracotta, wool,carpet, same-target no-op. Paintable entity first, then vanilla whitelist; existing remover adds paintable and six-GT-grass unpaint routes before its complete original reverse vanilla table. Hiss uses brokestar fire-extinguish placeholder, no nonexistent IC2 sound.",
    "Map brokestar six dyed grass variants to actual Source1 texture identities: Green→grassblock_medium,Lime→light,Black→dark,LightGray→normal,Yellow→yellow,Brown→brown. Brokestar GTGrassBlocks documents the medium/normal texture trap and exact dye indexes; preserve all existing Source1 ecology/grass/bale IDs, register no duplicate grass blocks. Ten other dyes decline grass color changes and any dyed variant removes to vanilla grass, exactly as donor routing.",
    "Adopt complete alive/non-sheared sheep and alive/tamed-wolf dyeing policy with different-color no-op and50 internal-unit payment. Preserve donor no owner requirement for a tamed wolf. Native private Wolf.setCollarColor uses a mapped Mixin invoker; Forge uses the same invoker contract rather than a reflective bridge. Entity painting happens on server, client returns success without writing color/ledger.",
    "One BlockEntityPaintMixin implements the shared state/contract on existing entities and restricts writes to gregtech namespace, avoiding another machine hierarchy. gt.color/gt.painted are saved through original superclass NBT, sent in vanilla update tags and immediate entity packets, chunk-dirty and model refresh triggered. Loader signatures stay in each platform. Non-GT entities cannot acquire paint. This extends paint ownership to existing GT block entities; it is a recorded integration policy, broader than importing only brokestar inherited machine base.",
    "Client-only BlockPaintColorMixin applies paint only to primary tint0; tint1 engine core and other overlays keep existing handlers. Unpainted surfaces use their original material handlers. ItemPaintColorMixin reads preserved BLOCK_ENTITY_DATA/native or BlockEntityTag/Forge on packed block items. Ordinary drops that already discard entity data are not silently changed into inventory-preserving drops. Existing container pack/clone NBT automatically includes paint where their serializer calls the superclass.",
    "Complete two original missing native vanilla hooks: WaterFluid.isSame now recognizes GT water family symmetrically using existing GTWorldWaterFluid and shared WaterMixinStatus; broken falling ore drops preserve original host stone and broken state/components through the full original EntityFallingOreDropMixin. Both native injections require their target and reuse existing water/ore registries; no new fluid/ore roots.",
    "Retain16 exact original brokestar texture PNGs and32 namespace-adapted original model aliases in shared core; add2 shared locale keys with vanilla translated dye names. Normalize original uppercase button hexadecimal underlay to lowercase resource identity on both consumers, preserving PNG bytes and source path/hash. One client-observed remaining forge:composite cap_nozzle model is subsequently isolated into original Forge/native loader boundary; alias exact original iconsets/void PNG to the existing missing block/void identity.51 resource records plus locale/mixin configuration boundaries are recorded."
  ],
